SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Tango After Midnight ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ This performance on Sunday July 5th 
 is **SOLD-OUT** }\n\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early July??\n\nWe'l
 l attend 'just' three performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details below.\n\n### 
 June 30-July 12\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th annual Toronto Fringe Fest
 ival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and performance. With [123 show
 s](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27 venues](https://fringeto
 ronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) across the city!\n\nSunda
 y July 5th (2pm-4pm)\n\n***TANGO After Midnight-- (55 minutes)***\n\nAs ni
 ght falls\, a new dance emerges...\n\nPointeTango—winner of the Toronto 
 Fringe Patrons’ Pick and the B Street Collaborative Dance Award—ignite
 s the stage with a striking fusion of pointe shoes and stilettos. This ele
 ctrifying production blends Argentine tango with classical ballet\, interw
 oven with cinematic projections filmed on location in Buenos Aires.\n\nFas
 t-paced and visually arresting\, the work features innovative lighting and
  sound design\, alongside world-class performers and 2025 Canadian Tango C
 hampions Erin Scott-Kafadar and Alexander Richardson.\n\n**A 15-time Fring
 e Award–winning company.**\n\n★★★★★ “Breathtaking artistry
 ” –Winnipeg Free Press\n★★★★★ “They dance as one body\, wi
 th grace and precision” –Monday Magazine\n\n**Ticket link here**--(our
  group will attend Sunday July 5th)\n\nhttps://fringetoronto.com/fringe/sh
 ow/tango-after-midnight\n\nDon't delay--Fringe tickets sell out quickly! $
 19 per person.
