SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Night Journey ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ This performance on July 7th is **SO
 LD-OUT**!! }\n\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early July??\n\nWe'll att
 end 'just' three performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details below.\n\n\\#\\#\\#
  June 30\\-July 12\\\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th annual Toronto Fringe
  Festival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and performance. With [123
  shows](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27 venues](https://fri
 ngetoronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) across the city!\n\n
 Tuesday July 7th (7pm-9pm) ***At the Arts & Letters Club!***\n\n**Night Jo
 urney-- (80 minutes)**\n\nThis original\, full-length play explores the dy
 namics among five strangers in a college night class studying the Greek ep
 ic\, The Odyssey. Each is broken in his or her own way\; all are in quest 
 of a better life. This challenging work of theatre is brought fully to lif
 e by Night Journey's exceptional cast of actors.\n\n**Performances are bei
 ng held at the beautiful Arts and Letters Club of Toronto\, 14 Elm St**. C
 ome early or stay late and enjoy the Club’s lounge or take a tour of our
  heritage building with its impressive collection of Canadian art.\n\n**Ti
 cket link here:** (our group will attend Tuesday July 7th)\n\nhttps://frin
 getoronto.com/fringe/show/night-journey\n\nDon't delay--Fringe tickets sel
 l out quickly! $19 per person.\n\nProducer: Martin Jones\, Renée Stein\, 
 Gregory Light\, with the assistance of members of the Arts and Letters Clu
 b **and six talented students from Toronto Metropolitan University’s Sch
 ool of Performance.**\n\nWe must support this!!
